# Build context hygiene for apps/api.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so everything in this directory used to be baked into the
# running image - including the SQLite database, the local virtualenv and the scratch reports.
# Anything that should never reach a container belongs here.
#
# NOTE ON `.env`: excluded, because docker-compose.yml now passes the API its own JWT_SECRET and
# SESSION_SECRET from the file next to it on the server. Before that change the container had no
# other source for a signing key, so the committed one came along in the image - which meant the
# key that mints admin tokens was readable by anyone with repository access.
#
# Sequencing matters if you are reading this on a server that is already running: create the
# `.env` next to docker-compose.yml first, then deploy. Compose stops with a named error if a
# `${VAR:?...}` is unset, and the API refuses to boot on a missing or previously-published
# secret; both are meant to be loud, not quiet.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Local data and generated reports - never part of an image.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
uploads/
scratch/
*.log
*cleanup*.json
*_report*.json
